From: Michal Kubecek <mkubecek@suse.cz>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:03:30 +0200
Subject: kabi: drop new skb drop reason SKB_BAD_GSO
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Patch-mainline: Never, kabi workaround
References: CVE-2026-53091 bsc#1269530

Backport of mainline commit 7fb4c1967011 ("net: pull headers in
qdisc_pkt_len_segs_init()") adds a new skb drop reason SKB_BAD_GSO which is
inserted into the middle of an enum, changing numeric value of existing
drop reason constants.

The easiest solution is revert the part introducing the new drop reason and
report generic REASON_NOT_SPECIFIED in places where it is set instead. As
drop reasons are only used for debugging purpose, this is not going to
cause any functional issues. To minimize deviation from mainline code,
preserve the SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO name but define it as equal to
SKB_DROP_REASON_NOT_SPECIFIED.

Signed-off-by: Michal Kubecek <mkubecek@suse.cz>
Reviewed-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
Reviewed-by: Michal Koutný <mkoutny@suse.com>
---
 include/net/dropreason-core.h | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/include/net/dropreason-core.h
+++ b/include/net/dropreason-core.h
@@ -56,7 +56,6 @@
 	FN(UNHANDLED_PROTO)		\
 	FN(SKB_CSUM)			\
 	FN(SKB_GSO_SEG)			\
-	FN(SKB_BAD_GSO)			\
 	FN(SKB_UCOPY_FAULT)		\
 	FN(DEV_HDR)			\
 	FN(DEV_READY)			\
@@ -259,8 +258,6 @@ enum skb_drop_reason {
 	SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_CSUM,
 	/** @SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_GSO_SEG: gso segmentation error */
 	SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_GSO_SEG,
-	/** @SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO: malicious gso packet. */
-	SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO,
 	/**
 	 * @SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_UCOPY_FAULT: failed to copy data from user space,
 	 * e.g., via zerocopy_sg_from_iter() or skb_orphan_frags_rx()
@@ -354,6 +351,15 @@ enum skb_drop_reason {
 	 */
 	SKB_DROP_REASON_MAX,
 
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
+	/**
+	 * SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO: malicious gso packet.
+	 * To avoid kABI breakage, this is defined as an alias for
+	 * SKB_DROP_REASON_NOT_SPECIFIED rather than a new drop reason.
+	 */
+	SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO = SKB_DROP_REASON_NOT_SPECIFIED,
+#endif
+
 	/**
 	 * @SKB_DROP_REASON_SUBSYS_MASK: subsystem mask in drop reasons,
 	 * see &enum skb_drop_reason_subsys
